Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns & potential usage  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."cpc": to find CPC symbols (filter those that start with ‘A61’)  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."assignee_harmonized": to extract normalised assignee names in whose portfolio we will count patents  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."publication_date": to derive the calendar year (busiest year)  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."country_code": 2‑letter jurisdiction of the publication (count top 5)  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."publication_number": basic identifier, handy for quick checks  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."family_id": family grouping if de‑duplication across authorities is later required (exploratory only)

Typical conditions  
1. LATERAL FLATTEN on "cpc" then WHERE c.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%' – keeps only the medical CPC group.  
2. LATERAL FLATTEN on "assignee_harmonized" to pull the string in the "name" key.  
3. (p."publication_date"/10000) AS pub_year – derives the year, keep it as INTEGER.  
4. GROUP BY pub_year / assignee / country_code to count, then ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC.

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑targeted SQL statements (all limited to 20 rows, all names double‑quoted).  

```sql
-- 1. Description: Look at a handful of CPC symbols to confirm format.
SELECT 
       p."publication_number",
       c.value:"symbol"::STRING          AS "cpc_symbol"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") c
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Inspect harmonised assignee objects and grab their names.
SELECT 
       a.value:"name"::STRING            AS "assignee_name",
       a.value                           AS "raw_assignee_obj"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Sample records that are classified in CPC starting with ‘A61’.
SELECT 
       p."publication_number",
       c.value:"symbol"::STRING          AS "cpc_symbol",
       p."country_code",
       p."publication_date"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") c
WHERE  c.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: List distinct harmonised assignees that have at least one A61 patent.
SELECT DISTINCT
       a.value:"name"::STRING            AS "assignee_name"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") c,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
WHERE  c.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Top‑20 assignees by raw patent count in A61 (helps locate “most active” one).
SELECT 
       a.value:"name"::STRING            AS "assignee_name",
       COUNT(*)                          AS "a61_patent_count"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") c,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
WHERE  c.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
GROUP  BY a.value:"name"::STRING
ORDER  BY COUNT(*) DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: For the leading assignee found above (replace %TOP_ASSIGNEE%), see yearly output volume.
SELECT 
       FLOOR(p."publication_date"/10000) AS "pub_year",
       COUNT(*)                           AS "a61_patent_count"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") c,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
WHERE  c.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
  AND  a.value:"name"::STRING ILIKE '%TOP_ASSIGNEE%'
GROUP  BY FLOOR(p."publication_date"/10000)
ORDER  BY COUNT(*) DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Confirm publications for that assignee during the busiest year (replace %BUSIEST_YEAR%).
SELECT 
       p."publication_number",
       p."country_code",
       p."publication_date"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") c,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
WHERE  c.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
  AND  a.value:"name"::STRING ILIKE '%TOP_ASSIGNEE%'
  AND  FLOOR(p."publication_date"/10000) = %BUSIEST_YEAR%
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Country‑level counts for that assignee in the busiest year.
SELECT 
       p."country_code",
       COUNT(*)                          AS "country_patent_count"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") c,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
WHERE  c.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
  AND  a.value:"name"::STRING ILIKE '%TOP_ASSIGNEE%'
  AND  FLOOR(p."publication_date"/10000) = %BUSIEST_YEAR%
GROUP  BY p."country_code"
ORDER  BY COUNT(*) DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Pull the top 5 jurisdiction codes for that assignee / year.
SELECT 
       p."country_code",
       COUNT(*)                          AS "country_patent_count"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") c,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
WHERE  c.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
  AND  a.value:"name"::STRING ILIKE '%TOP_ASSIGNEE%'
  AND  FLOOR(p."publication_date"/10000) = %BUSIEST_YEAR%
GROUP  BY p."country_code"
ORDER  BY COUNT(*) DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

```sql
--10. Description: Final composition – comma‑separated list of the 5 most‑used jurisdiction codes
--                by the most‑active A61 assignee in their busiest year.
WITH a61_data AS (
    SELECT 
           a.value:"name"::STRING        AS assignee_name,
           FLOOR(p."publication_date"/10000) AS pub_year,
           p."country_code"
    FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
           LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") c,
           LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
    WHERE  c.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
),
most_active AS (
    SELECT assignee_name
    FROM   a61_data
    GROUP  BY assignee_name
    ORDER  BY COUNT(*) DESC
    LIMIT 1
),
busiest_year AS (
    SELECT  pub_year
    FROM    a61_data d
    JOIN    most_active m
      ON    d.assignee_name = m.assignee_name
    GROUP   BY pub_year
    ORDER   BY COUNT(*) DESC
    LIMIT   1
)
SELECT 
       LISTAGG(country_code, ',')        WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY cnt DESC) AS top5_country_codes
FROM  (
       SELECT 
              d.country_code,
              COUNT(*) AS cnt
       FROM   a61_data d
       JOIN   most_active  m  ON d.assignee_name = m.assignee_name
       JOIN   busiest_year y  ON d.pub_year      = y.pub_year
       GROUP  BY d.country_code
       ORDER  BY cnt DESC
       LIMIT 5
) q
LIMIT 20;
```
